Initial Product Backlog
- Producer logs into the system to manage the products
- Producer creates a new product listing for customers
- Producer can enter product details (name, description, category, price, available quantity, availability period, farm origin)
- Producer can provide optional product info (harvest date, allergens, best-before date)
- Producer needs the system to validate required fields so incomplete listings can't be published
- Producer wants validation error messages
- Producer can declare a product as organically certified so customers can see
- System verifies organic cerifications through an external service
- Producer wants to be notified when verification fails so information can be corrected
- System handles external service failures so submissions aren't lost
- System publishes validated products automatically so customers can view
- Customer can see published products only once validation checks have passed
- Producer can update stock quantities so inventory is accurate
- Producer can update seasonal availability dates 
- System needs products to become unavailable when stock reaches 0 so customers can't order them
- System makes products available again when stock is resupplied
- Producer can view the current status of products (available, out of stock, pending verification)
- System can log validation and verification failures for troubleshooting
